      "role": "user",
      "tokenCount": 1081,
      "createTime": "2026-05-07T13:25:40.028Z"
    }, {
      "text": "This is a **Jinja syntax error**! Sometimes, when Jinja template tags (like `{% if %}`) are placed on the exact same line as HTML tags (like `\u003ca\u003e`), Python gets confused during the copy-paste process or your code editor accidentally auto-completes an extra `\u003e` character.\n\nLet\u0027s fix this by separating the Jinja tags from the HTML tags onto their own lines.\n\n### How to fix it:\nOpen your `teacher.html` file and look around **Line 68-71**. \n\nFind this block of code:\n```html\n        \u003cform action\u003d\"/teacher\" method\u003d\"POST\" class\u003d\"form-inline\" style\u003d\"border-left-color: #9e9e9e;\"\u003e\n            \u003clabel\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFilter Date:\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/label\u003e\n            \u003cinput type\u003d\"date\" name\u003d\"selected_date\" value\u003d\"{{ selected_date }}\"\u003e\n            \u003cbutton type\u003d\"submit\" class\u003d\"btn-blue\"\u003eFilter\u003c/button\u003e\n            {% if selected_date %\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/teacher\" class\u003d\"btn-gray\"\u003eShow All\u003c/a\u003e{% endif %}\n        \u003c/form\u003e\n```\n\n**Replace that entire block with this spaced-out version:**\n```html\n        \u003cform action\u003d\"/teacher\" method\u003d\"POST\" class\u003d\"form-inline\" style\u003d\"border-left-color: #9e9e9e;\"\u003e\n            \u003clabel\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFilter Date:\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/label\u003e\n            \u003cinput type\u003d\"date\" name\u003d\"selected_date\" value\u003d\"{{ selected_date }}\"\u003e\n            \u003cbutton type\u003d\"submit\" class\u003d\"btn-blue\"\u003eFilter\u003c/button\u003e\n            \n            {% if selected_date %}\n                \u003ca href\u003d\"/teacher\" class\u003d\"btn-gray\"\u003eShow All\u003c/a\u003e\n            {% endif %}\n            \n        \u003c/form\u003e\n```\n\n### Try testing again:\n1. Save `teacher.html`.\n2. You **do not** need to restart the Python server when you only change HTML files! \n3. Just go to your web browser and refresh the page (`http://127.0.0.1:5000/teacher`).\n\nIt should load perfectly now! Let me know if it displays the Admin Panel properly.",
      "role": "model",
