      "createTime": "2026-05-08T04:59:20.504Z"
    }, {
      "text": "This is the final piece of the puzzle! We will use the **LINE Messaging API** to send automatic alerts to LINE whenever a student borrows or returns a book.\n\nSince LINE Notify is shutting down soon, we are using the modern **LINE Bot (Messaging API)**, which is future-proof.\n\nHere is how we integrate it into your local Python app.\n\n### Step 1: Install `requests`\nWe need a library to let Python talk to the internet. Open your terminal, stop the server (`CTRL + C`), and run:\n```bash\npip install requests\n```\n\n### Step 2: Update `app.py`\nOpen `app.py`. We need to add the `requests` library, set up your LINE Token, and create a function to send the messages.\n\n**1. At the very top of `app.py`, update your imports:**\n```python\nfrom flask import Flask, render_template, request, redirect, url_for, session, flash\nfrom datetime import datetime\nimport sqlite3\nimport requests  # \u003c-- ADD THIS\n```\n\n**2. Right below `app.secret_key \u003d ...`, add your LINE credentials and the send function:**\n```python\napp \u003d Flask(__name__)\napp.secret_key \u003d \u0027mother_school_secret_key\u0027\n\n# --- LINE API SETTINGS ---\n# We will leave these blank for a moment, you will fill them in Step 3!\nLINE_ACCESS_TOKEN \u003d \u0027YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN\u0027\nLINE_TARGET_ID \u003d \u0027YOUR_USER_OR_GROUP_ID\u0027 \n\ndef send_line_alert(message):\n    if LINE_ACCESS_TOKEN \u003d\u003d \u0027YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN\u0027:\n        return # Do nothing if Token is not set yet\n        \n    url \u003d \u0027https://api.line.me/v2/bot/message/push\u0027\n    headers \u003d {\n        \u0027Content-Type\u0027: \u0027application/json\u0027,\n        \u0027Authorization\u0027: f\u0027Bearer {LINE_ACCESS_TOKEN}\u0027\n    }\n    data \u003d {\n        \"to\": LINE_TARGET_ID,\n        \"messages\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": message}]\n    }\n    try:\n        requests.post(url, headers\u003dheaders, json\u003ddata)\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"LINE API Error: {e}\")\n# -------------------------\n```\n\n**3. Update the `/borrow` route to trigger the alert:**\nFind your `/borrow` route and add the LINE alert right after `conn.commit()`:\n```python\n        # 1. Mark book as borrowed\n        conn.execute(\u0027UPDATE books SET status \u003d \"Borrowed\" WHERE book_id \u003d ?\u0027, (book_id,))\n        # 2. Save to daily logs\n        conn.execute(\u0027INSERT INTO logs (user_id, book_id, action) VALUES (?, ?, ?)\u0027, (user_id, book_id, \u0027Borrow\u0027))\n        conn.commit()\n        \n        flash(f\"✅ Successfully borrowed: {book[\u0027title\u0027]}\")\n        \n        # --- SEND LINE ALERT ---\n        alert_msg \u003d f\"📚 แจ้งเตือนห้องสมุด:\\nนักเรียน {session[\u0027user_name\u0027]} ได้ทำการ [ยืม] หนังสือ\\n📖 \u0027{book[\u0027title\u0027]}\u0027\"\n        send_line_alert(alert_msg)\n```\n\n**4. Update the `/return` route to trigger the alert:**\nFind your `/return` route and add the LINE alert right after `conn.commit()`:\n```python\n    conn.commit()\n    conn.close()\n    \n    flash(\"✅ Books successfully returned!\")\n    \n    # --- SEND LINE ALERT ---\n    alert_msg \u003d f\"✅ แจ้งเตือนห้องสมุด:\\nนักเรียน {session[\u0027user_name\u0027]} ได้ทำการ [คืน] หนังสือจำนวน {len(returned_book_ids)} เล่ม\"\n    send_line_alert(alert_msg)\n    \n    return redirect(url_for(\u0027student_dashboard\u0027))\n```\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Get your LINE Credentials\nTo make this actually work, you need to get a Token from LINE.\n\n1. Go to the [LINE Developers Console](https://developers.line.biz/console/) and log in with your normal LINE account.\n2. Click **Create a New Provider** (name it \"SchoolLibrary\").\n3. Click **Create a new channel** -\u003e Select **Messaging API**.\n4. Fill in the Bot\u0027s name (e.g., \"LSMS Bot\") and create it.\n5. Once created, click on the **Messaging API** tab. \n    * Scroll down to the QR code and scan it with your phone to add the Bot as a friend!\n6. Click on the **Basic Settings** tab.\n    * Scroll to the very bottom to find **\"Your user ID\"** (it starts with a `U...`). Copy this.\n    * *Paste this into `app.py` as your `LINE_TARGET_ID`.*\n7. Click on the **Messaging API** tab again.\n    * Scroll to the bottom to **\"Channel access token (long-lived)\"** and click **Issue**. Copy this long text.\n    * *Paste this into `app.py` as your `LINE_ACCESS_TOKEN`.*\n\n### Step 4: Test it out!\n1. Start your Python server (`python app.py`).\n2. Log in as Alice (Student `S01`).\n3. Borrow a book (`B01`).\n4. **Check your phone!** Your bot should instantly send you a message: \n   \u003e 📚 แจ้งเตือนห้องสมุด:\n   \u003e นักเรียน Alice ได้ทำการ [ยืม] หนังสือ\n   \u003e 📖 \u0027The Little Prince\u0027\n\n*(Note: Currently, we are using your personal `User ID` to test. Once it works, you can easily switch `LINE_TARGET_ID` to a `Group ID` so it sends to a chat group instead of just you).*\n\nLet me know if the message pops up on your phone!",
