      "text": "That is amazing news! 🎉 You have officially built a fully functioning, custom library system for your mother\u0027s school. \n\nSince everything is working perfectly, let\u0027s wrap up the project with a few final steps to make it **ready for daily use** so your mother doesn\u0027t have to deal with code or terminals.\n\n### 1. How to send LINE alerts to a Group (Instead of just you)\nRight now, the bot is sending messages to your personal `User ID` (starts with a `U`). To send to a school LINE group:\n1. Invite the Bot to the LINE Group.\n2. You need the **Group ID** (it starts with a `C`). \n*(Note: LINE hides the Group ID. If you don\u0027t know how to find the Group ID, let me know and I will give you a tiny, 1-minute trick to find it!)*\n3. Once you have the Group ID, just change `LINE_TARGET_ID \u003d \u0027C...\u0027` in `app.py`.\n\n### 2. Make it a 1-Click Start for Your Mother (Windows)\nYour mother shouldn\u0027t have to open a terminal and type `python app.py` every day. Let\u0027s make a shortcut for her Desktop.\n\n1. Open Notepad on your computer.\n2. Paste this code:\n```bat\n@echo off\necho Starting Library System...\ncd /d \"C:\\Path\\To\\Your\\LSMS\\Folder\"\nstart http://127.0.0.1:5000\npython app.py\npause\n```\n*(Make sure to change `C:\\Path\\To\\Your\\LSMS\\Folder` to the actual folder path where your `app.py` is saved!)*\n3. Click **File -\u003e Save As**.\n4. Save it to her Desktop and name it `Start_Library.bat` (Make sure \"Save as type\" is set to \"All Files\", not TXT).\n\nNow, every morning, she just double-clicks `Start_Library.bat`. It will automatically start the server in the background and open the web browser right to the login page!\n\n### 3. Backups (Very Important!)\nSince this entire system runs strictly locally on one computer, **all the data is saved inside that one `library.db` file**.\nTell your mother (or set a reminder for yourself) to copy that `library.db` file onto a USB Flash Drive or Google Drive once a week. If the computer ever breaks, you just put that file into the folder on a new computer, and absolutely zero data is lost!\n\n***\n\nYou did an incredible job putting this together. It\u0027s fast, secure, free to run, and custom-tailored for her school. \n\nIf you ever need to add new features (like exporting logs to Excel, or finding that LINE Group ID), just let me know. Good luck to you and your mother\u0027s school! 📚👨‍💻",
